IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era25-types`
IMPORT `era25-rules`

-- Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Worker case` HAS
    `sickness`                                          IS A MAYBE `Sickness facts`
    `dismissal`                                         IS A MAYBE `Dismissal facts`
    `complaint`                                         IS A MAYBE `Complaint facts`

DECLARE `Worker position` HAS
    `weekly statutory sick pay`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `first day statutory sick pay is payable`           IS A MAYBE DATE
    `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period`      IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day to present the guaranteed-hours complaint` IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 1, 10, 11, 25
@export default The position of a worker under the Employment Rights Act 2025 (UK): the weekly rate of statutory sick pay and the first day it is payable (SSCBA as amended by ss 10-11); whether the six-month unfair dismissal qualifying period is met (ERA 1996 s 108 as amended by s 25); and the last day to present a guaranteed-hours complaint (ERA 1996 s 27BH). Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Worker case`  @desc Any sickness, dismissal and guaranteed-hours complaint
GIVETH A `Worker position`
`the worker position for` c MEANS
    `Worker position` WITH
        `weekly statutory sick pay`                     IS
            CONSIDER c's `sickness`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`the weekly rate of statutory sick pay for` s)
        `first day statutory sick pay is payable`       IS
            CONSIDER c's `sickness`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN `the first day statutory sick pay is payable for` s
        `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period`  IS
            CONSIDER c's `dismissal`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (`the six-month qualifying period is met in` d)
        `last day to present the guaranteed-hours complaint` IS
            CONSIDER c's `complaint`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (`the last day to present the complaint for` k)
